.TH QLDAPPASSWD 1 "2026-09-29" "Qore OpenLDAP 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qldappasswd \- change an LDAP password
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qldappasswd
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This command uses Qore's OpenLDAP bindings to change an LDAP password.
Use --help for command-specific arguments and examples.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -H , --uri=URI
LDAP server URI; defaults to ldap://localhost:389.
.TP
.BR -D , --binddn=DN
Distinguished name for simple authentication.
.TP
.BR -W , --prompt-bind
Read the bind password without echoing it.
.TP
.BR -w , --passwd=PASSWORD
Specify a bind password. Prefer the prompt to keep passwords out of process arguments.
.TP
.BR -Z , --starttls
Negotiate TLS before authenticating.
.TP
.BR -v , --verbose
Show operation details. Bind passwords are redacted from search options.
.TP
.BR -C , --no-color
Disable terminal colors.
.TP
.BR -h , --help
Display complete usage information.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ldapsearch (1),
.BR qore (1)
The API reference is supplied by qore-openldap-module-doc.
